```sh
sh scripts/test.sh                                         # unit tests, -race, with an 80% coverage floor
[% if has_cli %]
go test ./internal/config -run Env                         # a subset, no coverage floor
[% else %]
go test -run Version .                                     # a subset, no coverage floor
[% endif %]
go test -tags integration ./tests/integration/...          # integration tests (real external systems)
```

CI runs the unit tests on every supported Go version, together with golangci-lint, go vet, `go mod tidy -diff`, the wiki checks and the manifest checks. All of them block a merge.
[% if integration_ci %]

The **Integration tests** job runs the integration tests too, with every package in `contrib/system-packages.txt`. It fails if no test passes or one is skipped, so a missing package or device fails it rather than passing it.
[% endif %]
